ormance-issues","content":"**Limit data points**: Consider pagination or filtering for very large datasets (>100 points)"},"1748":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-89","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#performance-issues","content":"**Debounce resize**: The default 15ms debounce on `useParentSize` balances smoothness and performance"},"1749":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart-90","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/bar-chart#performance-issues","content":"**Simplify tooltips**: If tooltips are complex, consider using simpler content or disabling them"},"1750":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","type":"page","content":"DonutChart","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components","Chart"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart"},"1751":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-0","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","content":"Donut charts are for parts-to-whole comparison—how partial elements add up to a total—shown as a ring so a few categories are easy to compare at a glance."},"1752":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-1","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#installation","content":"Installation"},"1753":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-2","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#examples","content":"Examples"},"1754":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-3","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#default","content":"Default"},"1755":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-4","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#single-slice","content":"Single slice"},"1756":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-5","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#legend-placement","content":"Legend placement"},"1757":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-6","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#small-slices","content":"Small slices"},"1758":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-7","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#format-value","content":"Format value"},"1759":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-8","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#props","content":"Props"},"1760":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-9","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#donutchart","content":"DonutChart"},"1761":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-10","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#default","content":"You give the chart a `data` array (`id`, `name`, `value`) and a `label` in the middle - this is the everyday setup when you want several categories on one ring and a headline number or title in the hole."},"1762":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-11","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#single-slice","content":"When there is only one slice, the ring is full. Add `subLabel` if you want a smaller second line under the main center text."},"1763":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-12","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#legend-placement","content":"Switch `legend` to `right` to sit the legend beside the donut, or `bottom` to stack it underneath. `legendLabel` is there when you want a title above the legend items."},"1764":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-13","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#small-slices","content":"Very thin slices can be noisy to hover. Anything at or below `smallSliceThreshold` (default `0.05` of the total) is treated as “small,” and if those slices sit next to each other on the ring, one hover opens a single tooltip that lists the whole group."},"1765":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart-14","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/donut-chart#format-value","content":"Use `formatValue` when the raw numbers in the tooltip should read like money, counts with separators, or whatever your product expects. The percentage of the total still formats on its own; your function only shapes the value column."},"1766":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"page","content":"LineChart","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components","Chart"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart"},"1767":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-0","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","content":"Line Chart shows how something changes over time or along a continuous scale. It connects data points with lines so people can quickly spot trends, peaks, dips, and patterns."},"1768":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-1","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#installation","content":"Installation"},"1769":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-2","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#examples","content":"Examples"},"1770":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-3","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#default","content":"Default"},"1771":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-4","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#multiple-series","content":"Multiple series"},"1772":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-5","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#gridlines","content":"Gridlines"},"1773":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-6","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#titles","content":"Titles"},"1774":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-7","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#labels","content":"Labels"},"1775":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-8","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#ticks","content":"Ticks"},"1776":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-9","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#baselines","content":"Baselines"},"1777":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-10","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#legend","content":"Legend"},"1778":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-11","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#axis-and-tooltip-formatting","content":"Axis and tooltip formatting"},"1779":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-12","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#custom-accessors","content":"Custom accessors"},"1780":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-13","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#missing-values","content":"Missing values"},"1781":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-14","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#fixed-domain","content":"Fixed domain"},"1782":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-15","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#nice-values","content":"Nice values"},"1783":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-16","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#zero-included","content":"Zero included"},"1784":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-17","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#custom-ticks","content":"Custom ticks"},"1785":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-18","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#band-padding","content":"Band padding"},"1786":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-19","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#tooltip-disabled","content":"Tooltip disabled"},"1787":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-20","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#crosshair-only","content":"Crosshair only"},"1788":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-21","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#custom-tooltip-formatting","content":"Custom tooltip formatting"},"1789":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-22","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#fixed-size","content":"Fixed size"},"1790":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-23","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#bitcoin-price","content":"Bitcoin price"},"1791":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-24","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#city-temperature","content":"City temperature"},"1792":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-25","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#browser-usage","content":"Browser usage"},"1793":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-26","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#rtl","content":"RTL"},"1794":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-27","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#color-index","content":"Color Index"},"1795":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-28","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#custom-tooltip","content":"Custom Tooltip"},"1796":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-29","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#custom-tooltip-pair-change","content":"Custom Tooltip Pair Change"},"1797":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-30","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#custom-tooltip-period-comparison","content":"Custom Tooltip Period Comparison"},"1798":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-31","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#line-styles","content":"Line Styles"},"1799":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-32","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#customization","content":"Customization"},"1800":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-33","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#data-attributes","content":"Data Attributes"},"1801":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-34","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#component-customization","content":"Component Customization"},"1802":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-35","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"1803":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-36","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#aria-support","content":"ARIA Support"},"1804":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-37","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#best-practices","content":"Best Practices"},"1805":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-38","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#when-to-use-linechart","content":"When to Use LineChart"},"1806":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-39","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"1807":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-40","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#chart-not-sizing-or-empty","content":"Chart Not Sizing or Empty"},"1808":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-41","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#dates-not-displaying-correctly","content":"Dates Not Displaying Correctly"},"1809":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-42","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#tooltip-or-crosshair-not-showing","content":"Tooltip or Crosshair Not Showing"},"1810":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-43","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#props","content":"Props"},"1811":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-44","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#linechart","content":"LineChart"},"1812":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-45","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#default","content":"One line, a time-scale X axis, and almost nothing else configured - the everyday starting point. You give the chart a `series` array and it reads `x`/`y` from each point."},"1813":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-46","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#multiple-series","content":"Several lines sharing one X axis, with a legend naming each of them. Reach for this when the comparison between series is the story."},"1814":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-47","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#gridlines","content":"`xGridlines` and `yGridlines` add faint lines across the plot so it is easier to read a value back off an axis."},"1815":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-48","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#titles","content":"`xTitle` and `yTitle` label what each axis actually measures, e.g. \"Month\" and \"Temperature (°F)\"."},"1816":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-49","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#labels","content":"`xLabels` and `yLabels` toggle the tick labels on each axis. Turn them off for sparklines or when the surrounding UI already names the values."},"1817":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-50","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#ticks","content":"`xTickMarks` and `yTickMarks` draw the short lines at each tick value, which helps tie a label to its exact position on the axis."},"1818":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-51","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#baselines","content":"`xBaseline` and `yBaseline` control the main axis lines themselves. Dropping them gives a lighter, more editorial chart."},"1819":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-52","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#legend","content":"`legendPosition` puts the legend above or below the plot, or hides it with `null`. Multi-series charts get a bottom legend by default."},"1820":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-53","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#axis-and-tooltip-formatting","content":"`xTickFormat` and `yTickFormat` shape the axis labels - dates, currency, units, percentages - and the tooltip follows the same formatting."},"1821":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-54","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#custom-accessors","content":"When your data does not use `x`/`y`, point `xAccessor` and `yAccessor` at the fields it does use (here `date` and `value`) instead of reshaping the data first."},"1822":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-55","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#missing-values","content":"A `null` Y value breaks the line instead of drawing through the gap, so missing data reads as missing rather than as a straight interpolation."},"1823":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-56","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#fixed-domain","content":"`xDomain` and `yDomain` pin the visible range. Use them to keep a fixed scale, or to keep several charts comparable."},"1824":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-57","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#nice-values","content":"`xNice` and `yNice` round the domain out to friendlier numbers (e.g. 0.2 to 1.0), so ticks land on values people expect."},"1825":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-58","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#zero-included","content":"`xZero` and `yZero` stretch the domain to include zero. Worth doing when the absolute size of the values matters, not just their movement."},"1826":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-59","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#custom-ticks","content":"Choose the ticks yourself with `xTickValues`/`yTickValues`, or just ask for roughly how many you want with `xNumTicks`/`yNumTicks`."},"1827":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-60","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#band-padding","content":"`xPaddingOuter` and `yPaddingOuter` add breathing room at the ends of a band or point scale so the first and last values are not pinned to the edges."},"1828":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-61","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#tooltip-disabled","content":"Turn off the hover affordances entirely with `tooltip={false}`, `showCrosshair={false}`, and `showDataPoints={false}` - useful for a static or print-style chart."},"1829":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-62","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#crosshair-only","content":"Keep the vertical crosshair for orientation while hiding the tooltip and the data point glyphs."},"1830":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-63","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#custom-tooltip-formatting","content":"`tooltipValueFormatter` shapes only the tooltip values, so you can show full currency or units there while the axis stays compact."},"1831":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-64","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#fixed-size","content":"Pass `width` and `height` to size the chart explicitly instead of letting it fill its container."},"1832":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-65","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#bitcoin-price","content":"A real time series: date formatting on the X axis, currency on the Y axis, gridlines, and a nice-rounded domain."},"1833":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-66","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#city-temperature","content":"Several cities over the same period, with a legend and a shared time axis - the multi-series case as it usually looks in a product."},"1834":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-67","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#browser-usage","content":"A categorical X axis (band scale) with several series and percentage formatting, for when the X values are names rather than numbers or dates."},"1835":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-68","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#rtl","content":"The chart follows the current layout direction, normally detected from the browser or system settings. In right-to-left it mirrors the axes and labels; this example forces RTL so you can see it in a left-to-right page."},"1836":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-69","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#color-index","content":"`colorIndex` pins each series to a palette color. Any series can use any index,\nindependently — here two pairs each share an index so an actual line and its\ndashed forecast read as the same color, distinguished only by line style."},"1837":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-70","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#custom-tooltip","content":"`renderTooltip` lets you render a fully custom tooltip and know which curve is\nhovered. Paired series share a `colorIndex`; hovering either line shows a\ntooltip specific to that line, wrapped in the default styled popover."},"1838":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-71","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#custom-tooltip-pair-change","content":"`renderTooltip` example combining a pair of series. Each pair shares a `colorIndex`\n(solid actual + dashed forecast); hovering either line shows the percent change of\nthe forecast against the actual for that pair, wrapped in the default styled popover."},"1839":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-72","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#custom-tooltip-period-comparison","content":"`renderTooltip` example styled as a period-over-period comparison card. Paired series\n(solid current period + dashed previous period) share a `colorIndex`; hovering either\nline shows both dated values and the percent change, wrapped in the default popover."},"1840":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-73","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#line-styles","content":"`variant` sets each series' line style — 'solid' (default), 'dashed', or\n'dotted' — useful for distinguishing actuals from forecasts or targets. The\nlegend swatch mirrors each line's style."},"1841":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-74","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#data-attributes","content":"The chart root exposes data attributes that reflect prop state for styling:"},"1842":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-75","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#data-attributes","content":"**Chart container:** `data-width`, `data-height`, `data-x-labels`, `data-y-labels`, `data-x-labels-vertical`, `data-x-baseline`, `data-y-baseline`, `data-x-tick-marks`, `data-y-tick-marks`"},"1843":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-76","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#component-customization","content":"Use the `className` prop on the chart container to add or override styles:"},"1844":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-77","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#aria-support","content":"Provide &#x2A;*`aria-label`** to describe the chart (e.g. \"Monthly sales revenue from January to May 2024\")."},"1845":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-78","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#aria-support","content":"Use &#x2A;*`desc`** for a longer description rendered in the SVG `<desc>` for screen readers."},"1846":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-79","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#aria-support","content":"The component sets ARIA attributes on interactive and structural elements as needed."},"1847":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-80","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#when-to-use-linechart","content":"Use for trends over time or along a continuous scale."},"1848":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-81","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#when-to-use-linechart","content":"Use when comparing a few series (e.g. 2-5 lines); avoid too many overlapping lines."},"1849":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-82","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#when-to-use-linechart","content":"Prefer a single chart with a legend over multiple small charts when comparing the same X range."},"1850":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-83","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#chart-not-sizing-or-empty","content":"Ensure the chart has a non-zero size. Place it in a container with explicit dimensions or use `width` and `height`:"},"1851":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-84","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#dates-not-displaying-correctly","content":"Use `xType=\"time\"` when the X-axis values are Date objects:"},"1852":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart-85","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/line-chart#tooltip-or-crosshair-not-showing","content":"Ensure `tooltip`, `showCrosshair`, or `showDataPoints` are not set to `false`, and that the chart receives pointer events (e.g. no overlay blocking hover)."},"1853":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","type":"page","content":"Gauge Chart","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components","Chart"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart"},"1854":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-0","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","content":"A visual indicator for representing a single quantitative value within a known range, rendered as a semicircle arc in continuous or segmented mode."},"1855":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-1","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#installation","content":"Installation"},"1856":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-2","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#examples","content":"Examples"},"1857":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-3","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#default","content":"Default"},"1858":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-4","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#continuous-values","content":"Continuous Values"},"1859":{"id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart-5","page_id":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/chart/gauge-chart#segmented","conte