red on the group container"],[1185,"`aria-label` required on the container for screen readers"],[355,"`aria-labelledby` associates the visible label when the `label` prop is provided"],[959,"`aria-labelledby` associates the visible label when the `label` prop is provided"],[252,"`aria-required` when selection is required"],[1060,"`aria-required` when selection is required"],[353,"`aria-valuemin` and `aria-valuemax` define the range (default `0`–`100`)"],[957,"`aria-valuemin` and `aria-valuemax` define the range (default `0`–`100`)"],[956,"`aria-valuenow` reflects the current value"],[352,"`aria-valuenow` reflects the current value (clamped to 0–100)"],[958,"`aria-valuetext` provides a formatted string (e.g. `\"60%\"`)"],[354,"`aria-valuetext` provides a formatted string (e.g. `\"60%\"`) via `Intl.NumberFormat`; the same string is rendered inside the circle. Override the text with the `aria-valuetext` prop, or control formatting with `formatOptions`"],[1891,"`Box` is a polymorphic layout component that renders as any HTML element or custom component via the `as` prop. It provides consistent spacing, elevation, rounding, and self-alignment within flex or grid containers."],[121,"`Calendar` values are `CalendarDate` objects. Import the date primitives you need from the `@godaddy/antares/date` subpath:"],[237,"`CheckboxGroup` is composed: write `Label`, a `Group` holding the `Checkbox` items, `Text slot=\"description\"`, and `FieldError`. The `Group` takes its axis, gap, and presentational role from the group's `orientation`, so a bare `<Group>` is all you need; pass your own `direction`/`gap` to lay the items out differently. Each `Checkbox` takes label text next to the indicator."],[307,"`ChipButton` for menu filters and other actions with a Chip-like appearance"],[325,"`ChipButton` is a real button and exposes menu state through `MenuTrigger`; provide an accessible name when the visible content is incomplete."],[303,"`ChipGroup` + `ChipList` + `Chip` for grouped values, selection, keyboard navigation, and removal"],[318,"`ChipGroup` owns selection and removal behavior. Use a Chip render prop for\nstate-dependent content, and `Button` with `slot=\"remove\"` together with\n`onRemove` for removable items. See **Toggle Chips** and **Removable Chips**."],[1617,"`className` and `style` apply to the tooltip panel."],[1836,"`colorIndex` pins each series to a palette color. Any series can use any index,\nindependently — here two pairs each share an index so an actual line and its\ndashed forecast read as the same color, distinguished only by line style."],[993,"`currentStep` is the single source of truth for the timeline. Omit it for a not-yet-started flow where every step is `future`; pass the step count for a fully completed flow where every step is `past`."],[584,"`data-color`: Applied when color prop is set"],[587,"`data-flip`: Applied when flip prop is set (\"horizontal\" or \"vertical\")"],[583,"`data-icon`: The icon name (always present)"],[585,"`data-loading`: Applied during icon loading from CDN"],[586,"`data-mode`: Applied when mode prop is set (e.g., \"sprite\")"],[588,"`data-rotate`: Applied when rotate prop is set (90, 180, or 270)"],[1293,"`data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focused`, `data-focus-visible`, `data-disabled`, `data-readonly`, `data-invalid`, `data-required`, `data-size`"],[382,"`DatePicker` (single) and `DateRangePicker` (range): a read-only formatted date label; the whole field opens a calendar popover"],[415,"`DrawerTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Drawer>`, handling open\nstate automatically."],[905,"`Enter/Space`"],[457,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[678,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[424,"`Escape`"],[862,"`Escape`"],[907,"`Escape`"],[1622,"`Escape`"],[494,"`FileTrigger` adds no visuals or ARIA of its own — accessibility comes from the pressable child you provide. Use a component with an accessible name (e.g. an Antares `Button` with clear label text) so assistive technology announces the action. The underlying `<input>` is visually hidden but remains operable by keyboard through the child's press behavior."],[1928,"`Flex` is a one-dimensional layout component for arranging children in rows or columns with alignment and spacing control. It extends `Box`, inheriting all `Box` capabilities (padding, elevation, rounding, self-alignment, and polymorphic `as` prop)."],[592,"`focusable=\"false\"`: Prevents keyboard focus"],[1966,"`Grid` is a two-dimensional CSS Grid layout component for complex grid-based layouts. It extends `Box`, inheriting all `Box` capabilities (padding, elevation, rounding, self-alignment, and polymorphic `as` prop)."],[508,"`Heading` renders a semantic `h1`-`h6` element via the `level` prop.\nInside a `Modal`/`Dialog`, add `slot=\"title\"` and it labels the dialog automatically."],[169,"`href` turns the Card into a native link. Modifier-click, middle-click, and \"Open in new tab\" work\non the surface. Body text is not selectable. The link covers the whole Card, so do not put\nCornerActions, buttons, inputs, selection, or other controls in an `href` Card. Clicking body text\non an `onPress` or selection Card activates it; dragging that text selects it."],[666,"`InlineDrawerPanel` is the collapsible content for the accordion pattern — a thin wrapper over RAC `DisclosurePanel` that hides when collapsed. The trigger is any component you slot in with `slot=\"trigger\"` — there's no dedicated trigger component."],[695,"`Input` is the single-line control inside a field, not a field on its own. Prefer `TextField` or `NumberField` as the parent; see those components for fuller examples."],[163,"`isDisabled` disables the Card's primary action or selection and fades the whole Card. A\ndisabled CheckboxGroup or RadioGroup does the same. Read-only selection keeps its value visible."],[170,"`isDisabled` disables the primary action or selection and fades the Card. Controls you nest\ninside keep their own disabled state. Required and invalid state belong on `CheckboxGroup` or\n`RadioGroup`, and so does radio read-only state."],[1819,"`legendPosition` puts the legend above or below the plot, or hides it with `null`. Multi-series charts get a bottom legend by default."],[1897,"`lg` - Large spacing"],[724,"`ListBox` requires either `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`. For a labeled, popover-style picker, prefer `Select`."],[1896,"`md` - Medium spacing"],[759,"`MenuTrigger` exposes its open state via `isOpen`/`onOpenChange`,\nwhich can be used to drive the rotation of a chevron icon."],[119,"`minValue` / `maxValue` bounds and `isDateUnavailable` per-day disabling"],[385,"`minValue` / `maxValue` bounds and `isDateUnavailable` per-day disabling"],[857,"`Modal` accepts `isOpen` and `onOpenChange` directly, so it can be controlled without a\n`ModalTrigger`. Useful when the modal is opened from several places at once."],[853,"`ModalTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Modal>`, handling open state automatically. Based on RAC `DialogTrigger`."],[160,"`onPress` is the Card primary. Nested buttons keep their own hits, so Save does not open the\nModal. Compose a Card inside the Modal when the action is a focused form."],[992,"`orientation` switches between `horizontal` (accent bar on top) and `vertical` (accent bar on the leading edge)."],[1699,"`orientation=\"horizontal\"` swaps the axes: categories run down the side and values across the bottom. Reach for it when the labels are long or the chart is really a ranking."],[1362,"`overflowLabels` is optional and defaults to \"Previous tabs\" and \"Next tabs\". Provide localized labels when needed; they should describe the logical direction rather than physical directions like \"left\" or \"right\", as the component automatically handles RTL layouts."],[1612,"`overlay` elevation panel positioned relative to its trigger, with an optional arrow"],[686,"`placement` does not flip in RTL; the side is decided by document/flex order."],[669,"`placement` selects the collapse axis (`left`/`right` → width, `top`/`bottom` → height)"],[899,"`PopoverTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Popover>`, handling open state and positioning automatically.\nBased on RAC `DialogTrigger`. To anchor a popover to an element it doesn't wrap, pass `triggerRef` instead."],[672,"`prefers-reduced-motion` support"],[933,"`Pressable` accepts the React Aria press props, including `onPress`, `onPressStart`, `onPressEnd`, `onPressUp`, and `onPressChange`."],[938,"`Pressable` automatically applies React Aria state attributes such as `[data-hovered]`, `[data-pressed]`, `[data-focus-visible]`, and `[data-disabled]` to the child. Ensure the child component styles these states appropriately if it overrides the default `Pressable` styles."],[1047,"`RadioGroup` is composed: write `Label`, a `Group` holding the `Radio` items, `Text slot=\"description\"`, and `FieldError`. The `Group` takes its axis, gap, and presentational role from the group's `orientation`, so a bare `<Group>` is all you need; pass your own `direction`/`gap` to lay the items out differently. Each `Radio` takes label text next to the indicator. `orientation` also sets keyboard-navigation direction and ARIA."],[1838,"`renderTooltip` example combining a pair of series. Each pair shares a `colorIndex`\n(solid actual + dashed forecast); hovering either line shows the percent change of\nthe forecast against the actual for that pair, wrapped in the default styled popover."],[1839,"`renderTooltip` example styled as a period-over-period comparison card. Paired series\n(solid current period + dashed previous period) share a `colorIndex`; hovering either\nline shows both dated values and the percent change, wrapped in the default popover."],[1837,"`renderTooltip` lets you render a fully custom tooltip and know which curve is\nhovered. Paired series share a `colorIndex`; hovering either line shows a\ntooltip specific to that line, wrapped in the default styled popover."],[864,"`role=\"dialog\"` is applied automatically by the underlying React Aria `Dialog`"],[909,"`role=\"dialog\"` is applied automatically by the underlying React Aria `Dialog`"],[428,"`role=\"dialog\"` with `aria-modal=\"true\"` on the drawer panel (via RAC Modal)"],[591,"`role=\"img\"`: When title prop is provided"],[590,"`role=\"presentation\"`: For decorative icons"],[351,"`role=\"progressbar\"` on the container"],[955,"`role=\"progressbar\"` on the container"],[1057,"`role=\"radio\"` on each option"],[1182,"`role=\"radio\"` on each segment"],[1056,"`role=\"radiogroup\"` on the container"],[1181,"`role=\"radiogroup\"` on the container"],[1574,"`selectionMode=\"multiple\"` → `role=\"toolbar\"` on container, `role=\"button\"` + `aria-pressed` per item"],[1573,"`selectionMode=\"single\"` → `role=\"radiogroup\"` on container, `role=\"radio\"` + `aria-checked` per item"],[765,"`size` controls item density. Shown here as two standalone menus so both\nsizes are visible at once; in practice you set `size` on the `Menu` inside a\n`MenuTrigger`."],[1494,"`size` is the tier: the eyebrow reads it on the `detail` ramp, the title on `heading`,\nand the body on `body`. Use `2xl` for a page title, `xl` for a hero, `lg` for a section\ntitle, and `md` (the default) everywhere else."],[507,"`slot=\"title\"` inside a `Modal` or `Dialog` sets the accessible name."],[1895,"`sm` - Small spacing"],[799,"`Space` / `Enter`"],[1319,"`Space` toggles the switch when it has focus"],[994,"`status` is independent of timeline and only controls the status icon and (for `error`) the accent bar color."],[426,"`Tab`"],[455,"`Tab`"],[680,"`Tab`"],[797,"`Tab`"],[860,"`Tab`"],[1620,"`Tab`"],[1366,"`Tab`: `data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focus-visible`, and `data-disabled`."],[1363,"`TabList` must be rendered inside `Tabs` and must provide `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`. Give each `Tab` and its corresponding `TabPanel` the same `id`; React Aria uses that key to build their accessible relationship."],[1367,"`TabPanel`: `data-inert` when